  "windows": {
    "note": "Whether the host replaced the window as a whole, rather than growing or editing the one the reader is in. `previous` and `next` are the row keys (`clientMsgId || serverId`) of the window before and after one change, in timeline order. The window is replaced when both have rows and any of three holds: the host names its windows (`windowId`, the core timeline view's `viewId`; null or empty is no name) and the name changed from one name to another; the reader asked for the latest messages (`jumpRequested`, the back-to-latest key) and the new window is attached (`hasNewer` false); or no row of the new window was in the old one. A first window (`previous` empty) opens and an emptied one starts over; neither is a replacement. Rows that overlap without a new name are the same window changed: a page, an arrival, an edit, a removal, or a core snapshot of rows that are still there. What a replacement does to the list is in `locateAfterReplace`.",
